# nr-office-author-pptx-writer-package: what the lead applies (all of it is in files this task does not own).
# (No protocol rows, no daemon service, no SERVICE_PENDING change: the writer is a library module with no caller yet; the
# pptx build task (nr-office-author-pptx-build) is its caller.)

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-author/src/lib.rs
Add the module beside `pub mod brief;`:

    pub mod pptx_writer;

and extend the crate's header comment with one line: `pptx_writer`, the pptx package the `pptxgenjs` 4.0.1 library writes
for the calls of `authoring/pptx-html-build.mjs` (presentation, theme, master, layout, slides, shapes, pictures, notes).

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-author/Cargo.toml
[dependencies]: add, after the `mixdog-office-quality` line (both are workspace entries already):

    mixdog-ooxml = { workspace = true }
    base64 = { workspace = true }

(`mixdog-ooxml` for its `zipio::Package`, the container the package is built in; `base64` for the picture data. The twin
test `tests/twin_pptx_writer.rs` also reads `serde_json`, `base64` and `mixdog-office-base` (feature `test-support`), which
the crate lists already or with the two lines above.) The new edge mixdog-office-author -> mixdog-ooxml closes no cycle
(mixdog-ooxml depends on mixdog-office-base, mixdog-ooxml-text, mixdog-js, mixdog-fsio, mixdog-fonts and others, not on
the authoring crate).

## 3. native/core/Cargo.lock
The package `mixdog-office-author` gains the dependencies `base64` and `mixdog-ooxml` (both already in the lock; no new
external crate and no new feature of one). Lead regenerates it offline (`cargo update --workspace --offline`).

