## 5. For the later tasks of the track
The module exports `pptx_writer::{Presentation, Slide, Layout, Dim, ShapeOptions, Fill, Line, Shadow, Hyperlink,
ImageOptions, ImageFile, ImageSizing, SizingKind, Background, SlideNumber, SlideNumberMargin, ThemeFonts}`.
`Presentation::new`, `set_layout("LAYOUT_WIDE")` or `define_layout(name, inches, inches)` then `set_layout(name)`,
`add_slide() -> &mut Slide`, `Slide::{add_shape(preset, options), add_image(options), add_notes, set_background,
set_hidden}`, `Presentation::set_slide_number(index, props)`, `package() -> mixdog_ooxml::zipio::Package`, `write()`.
What the text writer (nr-office-author-pptx-writer-text) adds: a `SlideObject::Text` / table object in `slide.rs`
(`SlideObject` is the enum of a slide's objects in order; the id of an object on the slide is its place in it plus 2, a
notes object counts) and its `p:sp` / `p:graphicFrame` writer beside `shapes::shape_xml` (a shape carries `txBody` through
`genXmlTextBody`; `ShapeObject` has no text yet, so a framed text box is a `ShapeObject` with a text body field added
there). The chart writer (nr-office-author-pptx-charts) adds `rels_chart` to `Slide` (it counts in the next relationship
id, `Slide::next_rel_id`, and goes after the hyperlinks in `rels_xml`) and the chart Override of `content_types_xml`.
Not carried here, on purpose: audio/video (`addMedia`), SVG pictures (pptxgenjs's own SVG preview is a broken-image
placeholder), `defineSlideMaster`, sections (random ids), custom geometry points; gradients are not a pptxgenjs shape fill
(the chart/normalise task writes native gradients after the fact).
